    <comment>New package python-comfyui-workflow-templates-core for openSUSE:Factory from science:machinelearning (ComfyUI cone). pluskalm is the science:machinelearning package maintainer.

INTERDEPENDENT REQUESTS - please stage together (ComfyUI cone):
  * sr#1372780 python-trampoline
  * sr#1372737 python-av (devel:languages:python; Factory 14.2.0, need &gt;= 16 for comfyui)
  * remaining cone packages from science:machinelearning being submitted in this batch

Fri Aug 21 08:51:33 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal &lt;mpluskal@suse.com&gt;

- Initial package (version 0.3.315): core helpers (manifest loading
  and asset path resolution) for ComfyUI workflow templates.
</comment>
    <requestid>1372791</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>ac42252f277fbb9cef92fd0a77414921</srcmd5>
    <version>0.3.320</version>
    <time>1787656855</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.3.320.

The template manifest grows from 522 to 528 entries, adding the Bytedance
VCube video enhance, Meshy7 image/text to model and Wan 3.0 i2v/r2v/t2v API
templates. loader.py and __init__.py are byte-identical to 0.3.315.

PLEASE STAGE TOGETHER with the rest of this release train, submitted as
separate requests:
  sr#1373544  python-comfyui-workflow-templates-json           0.1.55
  sr#1373547  python-comfyui-workflow-templates-media-assets-01 0.1.33
  plus python-comfyui-workflow-templates 0.11.46 (request filed right after
  this one)

The set is only consistent together: the six templates this manifest adds
name assets that exist only in -json 0.1.55 and -media-assets-01 0.1.33, and
iter_assets() raises FileNotFoundError on the first missing asset. The
0.11.44 meta package additionally pins &quot;-core = 0.3.315&quot; exactly, so it goes
unresolvable if this lands alone; its request relaxes those pins to floors.

Note this package tracks the PyPI distribution
comfyui_workflow_templates_core, whose version lineage is separate from the
comfyui_workflow_templates meta package.

(Supersedes sr#1373545, which I revoked because it was submitted alone.)
</comment>
    <requestid>1373548</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>186521cbebd731f93dbcfa8b9ac199f2</srcmd5>
    <version>0.3.322</version>
    <time>1787766809</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update python-comfyui-workflow-templates-core to 0.3.322.

This package tracks its own PyPI distribution (comfyui_workflow_templates_core),
not the parent repository's 0.11.x version line. 0.3.322 is the current release
of that distribution.

The template manifest grows from 528 to 533 entries (Pixal3D/TRELLIS.2 image to
model, Nano Banana 2 image edit continuation, SDXL 1.0 simple text to image,
SAM 3D Body mesh extraction, MiniMax H3 image to video continuation); the
loader and the public helper API are unchanged.

Staging: these four requests must land in the SAME staging project -- the
meta package python-comfyui-workflow-templates 0.11.48 raises its
BuildRequires and Requires floors onto the three new bundle versions, so
splitting the batch across stagings leaves it unresolvable.

Sequencing: please stage this together with, or after, SR 1373695, which
converts comfyui's exact &quot;=&quot; pins on this package family to floors. Until
1373695 is accepted, Factory's comfyui still requires
python3XX-comfyui-workflow-templates = 0.11.44, so a staging that takes this
batch without 1373695 will show comfyui broken in installcheck. All four new
versions in this batch (0.11.48, 0.3.322, 0.1.57, 0.1.35) satisfy the floors
1373695 introduces, so no comfyui spec change is needed.

Submitted together with python-comfyui-workflow-templates 0.11.48,
python-comfyui-workflow-templates-json 0.1.57 and
python-comfyui-workflow-templates-media-assets-01 0.1.35.</comment>
    <requestid>1373737</requestid>
  </revision>
